## The two pins, per runtime

**`mtp_depth` = `off` | `1` | `2` | `3`** (vMLX's `cli.py:1662-1682, :4304-4331`; ceiling `native_mtp.py:28-44`). A depth is always passed as `--native-mtp-depth N --native-mtp-depth-policy fixed`, because the default policy is adaptive *within one request* (`cli.py:4324-4331`).

| runtime | absent / `off` | a depth |
|---|---|---|
| vmlx | `--disable-native-mtp` (the pre-pin command) | the depth + `fixed`, only after `vmlx_mtp_refusal` passes: family in `native_mtp.py:64-79`, nothing dropping MTP (`:883-925`), a declared layer (`:537-571`), `mtp.*` in the index (`:606-611`) |
| mlxlm | no flag — no MTP in the server (`'mtp'` absent from `server.py`, 23 options) | refused |
| optiq | same server underneath (`cli.py:2332, :2571, :3030`) | refused |
| omlx | no flag; the scratch holds no `model_settings.json` → `mtp_enabled` False (`model_settings.py:303`) | refused — `mtp_num_draft_tokens` is per-model and adaptive even when set (`:304-308`) |
| osaurus | accepted only at host `mtp.mode=force_off` (tracked key, read via the drift gate) | refused — `mtp.explicitDepth` is host state (`osaurus.md:344`) |

**`stream_experts` = `off` | `on`** (`STREAM_EXPERTS`; OptiQ's default is `auto`, `cli.py:2607-2615, :3095-3096`).

| runtime | absent / `off` | `on` |
|---|---|---|
| optiq | `--no-stream-experts` (`serve.py:1629-1630` is a complete opt-out) | `--stream-experts`, then the log check |
| vmlx | nothing (`--flash-moe` is `default=False`, `cli.py:3966`, `flash_moe_config.py:29`) | `--flash-moe`, then the log check |
| mlxlm | no flag — no expert path in `server.py` | refused |
| omlx | no flag | refused — burst decode (`settings.py:148-162`, `engine_core.py:176-188`) moves stream granularity, not expert residency |
| osaurus | accepted only at `concurrency.smeltMode=disabled` | refused — the enum (`engineSelected|disabled|flashMoE|ssdStreaming`) is host state |

## How "on" and a depth are verified

- **Depth**: at the artifact, before anything starts — `measure._visit` hands `mtp_depth_refusal` the cell's own `artifact_dir`, so a caller cannot omit the check. A bundle vMLX will not wire is `N/A` with the failed check named, never a depth cell decoded as plain autoregressive.
- **`on`**: after the start, before the first request. `Handle.log_path` (new field, set by `Runtime.start` to the file `_spawn` redirects into) is read from the head (`LOG_HEAD_BYTES = 1 MiB`). OptiQ needs **both** `[optiq.serve] SSD expert streaming: on` and `... pre-loaded` — the banner alone prints before the model is inspected (`cli.py:3095-3101`) — and vMLX needs `Flash MoE enabled:` (`server.py:8996-9002`, written at the readiness barrier ahead of `:6199`). Missing → `FAIL`, the first fallback line quoted (or "says nothing about why" when the log carries none), the start's own `cold_load_s`/`version` kept on the row, and the cell not revisited.

